STATES (every state renders — the label + field selector is ALWAYS present, never hidden behind a null
guard; the candidate-list chrome is layered under it so the selector stays usable in every state — the
correct UX for a form control, the same "native chrome around the web core" pattern accepted for siblings
0079/0269)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  loading  → label + field + a one-line skeleton ("Loading available signals…") while useSignals resolves
  content  → label + field; no extra chrome (web `options` present)
  empty    → label + field + a friendly "No signals are available for this vehicle yet" hint (web options=[])
  error    → label + field + an inline QueryError-equivalent with a Retry affordance (selector stays usable)
  stale    → a freshness banner above the selector + one guarded auto-refresh, cached field stays visible
  offline  → a freshness banner above the selector ("showing the last loaded signal list"), field visible

